{
  "info": {
    "name": "Smart Catalog API",
    "description": "Postman collection for the Smart Catalog Spring Boot API.\n\n## Quick start\n1. Set `baseUrl` (default `http://localhost:8080`), `username` and `password` in the collection **Variables** tab.\n2. Run **Auth › Register** (first time) or **Auth › Login**.\n3. The JWT is stored in the `token` variable automatically (global + collection) and sent as `Authorization: Bearer {{token}}` by every other request — no manual copying.\n\n`categoryId` / `productId` are filled in automatically by the Create requests.\n\n## Notes\n- All JSON responses use the envelope `{ status_code, message, error, body }`.\n- Rate limit: 20 requests/minute per user (per IP when unauthenticated). Exceeding it returns **429** with `X-RateLimit-Retry-After-Seconds`.\n- A missing/expired token returns **403** — just run Login again.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{token}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "event": [
    {
      "listen": "test",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "if ((pm.response.code === 401 || pm.response.code === 403) && !pm.info.requestName.match(/Login|Register/)) {",
          "    console.warn(\"Unauthorized — token missing or expired. Run Auth › Login to refresh {{token}}.\");",
          "}"
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:8080",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "username",
      "value": "testuser",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "password",
      "value": "password123",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "token",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "categoryId",
      "value": "1",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "productId",
      "value": "1",
      "type": "string"
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Auth",
      "description": "Public endpoints (`/auth/**`) — no JWT required.\n\nBoth requests store the returned JWT in the `token` variable automatically, so every other request in this collection is authenticated without any manual copy/paste.",
      "auth": {
        "type": "noauth"
      },
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Register",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/register",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "auth",
                "register"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Creates a new user (password stored as BCrypt hash) and returns a JWT — auto-login after register.\n\n- `username`: required\n- `password`: required, min 6 characters\n\nReturns **201** on success, **409** if the username is already taken (use **Login** instead).",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"username\": \"{{username}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{password}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"Request succeeded\", function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.be.success;",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "// Response envelope: { status_code, message, error, body: { token, message } }",
                  "const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "const token = json && json.body && json.body.token;",
                  "",
                  "if (token) {",
                  "    // Saved globally (as requested) and on the collection, so it wins over any",
                  "    // stale collection-level value — every request then sends Bearer {{token}}.",
                  "    pm.globals.set(\"token\", token);",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set(\"token\", token);",
                  "    console.log(\"JWT saved to {{token}}\");",
                  "} else {",
                  "    console.warn(\"No token found in response — token variable not updated.\");",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Login",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/login",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "auth",
                "login"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Authenticates existing credentials and returns a JWT.\n\nReturns **200** on success, **401** on invalid username/password.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"username\": \"{{username}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{password}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"Request succeeded\", function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.be.success;",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "// Response envelope: { status_code, message, error, body: { token, message } }",
                  "const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "const token = json && json.body && json.body.token;",
                  "",
                  "if (token) {",
                  "    // Saved globally (as requested) and on the collection, so it wins over any",
                  "    // stale collection-level value — every request then sends Bearer {{token}}.",
                  "    pm.globals.set(\"token\", token);",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set(\"token\", token);",
                  "    console.log(\"JWT saved to {{token}}\");",
                  "} else {",
                  "    console.warn(\"No token found in response — token variable not updated.\");",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
